            "SR6105d83870a1e737"
          ],
          "text": "The central legal question is whether, prior to the 1929 enactment of Section 65-A of the Transfer of Property Act, a mortgagor in possession had the power to grant a permanent lease of the mortgaged property so as to bind the mortgagee.",
          "refs": [
            "S34eef73a1804"
          ],
          "source_owner": "O64a6f8caf1b4a2e1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "T5224ab3cb1ca9fe9": {
      "uses": [
        {
          "state": "TRUE",
          "contribution": "The High Court held the 1925 permanent lease valid because it did not render the Bank's security insufficient under Section 66 of the Transfer of Property Act.",
          "limitations": [
            "SR34d2fe4ad826c718",
            "SR7a38facc11049cda"
          ],
          "content_role": "LEGAL_ASSESSMENT",
          "status": "COURT_RECORDED",
          "purpose": "REPORT_ASSERTION",
          "source_record_ids": [
            "SR34d2fe4ad826c718"
          ],
          "text": "The High Court negatived the contention regarding constructive res judicata. It considered whether Wazir Narayan Singh had power to grant the permanent lease, concluding the lease did not render the Bank's security insufficient under Section 66.",
          "refs": [
            "S2d91d1862dc2",
            "Sd3c548138ec6",
            "S978119f4c532"
          ],
          "source_owner": "Oc4f8cbb5279d28a3"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Tbc2183dd949a3b79": {
      "uses": [
        {
          "state": "TRUE",
          "contribution": "The trial court found the plaintiff was subrogated to the Bank's position and that the defendants were bound by the earlier mortgage decree.",
          "limitations": [
            "SR89feb810c247d711",
            "SR34d2fe4ad826c718"
          ],
          "content_role": "LEGAL_ASSESSMENT",
          "status": "COURT_RECORDED",
          "purpose": "REPORT_ASSERTION",
          "source_record_ids": [
            "SR89feb810c247d711"
          ],
          "text": "The Trial Court held the Plaintiff was subrogated to the Bank's position, Defendant 1 was the Manager/Karta, Defendant 2 was fully represented, the decree was binding, and the Plaintiff was entitled to recover possession and mesne profits.",
          "refs": [
            "S601d5df39aca"
          ],
          "source_owner": "Oc4f8cbb5279d28a3"
        }
      ]
    },
    "T9293e564b49a80fe": {
      "uses": [
        {
          "state": "TRUE",
          "contribution": "The defendants contended the plaintiff was not subrogated to the Bank's position and the lease was not ended by the auction sale.",
          "limitations": [
            "SR43b1f9b4f4974e70",
            "SR89feb810c247d711"
          ],
          "content_role": "ATTRIBUTION",
          "status": "PARTY_CLAIM",
          "purpose": "REPORT_ASSERTION",
          "source_record_ids": [
            "SR43b1f9b4f4974e70"
          ],
          "text": "Defendant 2 contended that the Plaintiff was not subrogated to the Bank's position, the decree was not binding as he was not a party, the Patta was not ended by the auction sale, and a partition occurred within a year allotting properties to him.",
          "refs": [
            "S2e0ba5982107",
            "Sf05a6bb45a8e",
            "Sd6e9439ddc2d"
          ],
          "source_owner": "Oc4f8cbb5279d28a3"
        }
      ]
    },
    "T1f19aaf057edba3d": {
      "uses": [
        {
          "state": "TRUE",
          "contribution": "The Privy Council has not yet delivered a final ruling on whether a pre-1929 permanent lease binds a subsequent mortgagee.",
          "limitations": [
            "SR7e1e94b77d6db4b4",
            "SR34d2fe4ad826c718"
          ],
          "content_role": "LEGAL_ASSESSMENT",
          "status": "COURT_RECORDED",
          "purpose": "REPORT_ASSERTION",
          "source_record_ids": [
            "SR7e1e94b77d6db4b4"
          ],
          "text": "The Privy Council found the Plaintiff was subrogated to the Bank's position and Defendant 2 was sufficiently represented. The only surviving question was whether Wazir Narayan Singh had the power to grant a permanent lease to bind the Plaintiff.",
          "refs": [
            "S3f8801f7bc98"
          ],
          "source_owner": "Oc4f8cbb5279d28a3"
        }
      ]
    },
